{"school":{"dbn":"22K381","name":"I. S. 381","boro":"Brooklyn","district":"22","district_label":"District 22","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":296,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"2500 NOSTRAND AVENUE, BROOKLYN, NY 11210","phone":"929-397-9200","website":"www.is381.org","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/64343","accessibility":"Not Accessible","overview":"I.S. 381 offers an intimate, personalized and nurturing environment for students, where academic rigor and excellence is valued. Our staff works collaboratively to develop enriched, rigorous and individualized curricula designed to meet the learning and developmental needs of students. IS 381 offers accelerated courses including Living Environment, Common Core Algebra and American History leading to Regents credits. Additionally, students participate in three separate academies as they move through each grade.  Our 6th Graders will enter into the Academy of Dramatic and Fine Arts (ADAFA).  Here our newest students will engage in a program dedicated to nurturing new and existing talents, while providing comprehensive instruction. It affords students the opportunity to pursue and develop their interests and talents through coursework, performances, showcases and/or galleries.  Our 7th Graders will participate in the Academy of Law and Civics. In this academy, students will be introduced to the many careers in the fields of law, the courts, and law enforcement. Enrichment courses will focus on various types of law and the study of legal issues, government, the courts, and law enforcement. Seventh grade students in the Law and Civics Academy will engage in role-playing activities surrounding important cases, learn public speaking skills and how forensics plays a part in law enforcement. Students in the Law and Civics academy will also visit our local courts, participate in fun law-themed trips, and have the opportunity to meet and work directly with court officials and law enforcement. Our 8th graders will participate in the Medical Science Academy which will prepare students to achieve success throughout high school. Students will gain relevant experience by attending local science museums, visiting nearby colleges offering STEAM majors, and visits to local medical facilities. Students will network with current medical and science professionals in order to gain insight to pathways and experiences in these fields.    Each of these academies offer enrichment coursework to prepare our students to enter prestigious programs in District 22 High Schools.  The school also has partnerships with several organizations including New York Edge, Girl Be Heard, and CHAMPS, which provide the school's morning and after school programs.  In addition, I.S. 381 offers a renowned \"STEAM\" Enrichment After School program that combines academics with activities that are geared at strengthening the social emotional learning capabilities of our students.  S for Sports, T for technology, E for Engineering, A for the Arts and M for Music. Our STEAM program has offerings including Flag football, STEM Design and Logo Club, Visual Arts, and Empower U/Nutrition to name a few.   The school participates in several Chancellor's initiatives: Algebra for All, College Access for All, Computer Science for All and Civics for All Partner Program as well.","start_time":"08:00am","end_time":"02:19pm","languages":null,"subway":null,"bus":"B11, B41, B44, B44-SBS, B49, B6, B7, B82, B82-SBS, B9, BM1, BM3, BM4","shared_building":"1","neighborhood":"Midwood","latitude":40.623804,"longitude":-73.946827,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":"2015-16","last_year":"2024-25"},"series":{"attendance_inperson_k8_all":{"y":["2020-21"],"v":[0.916],"st":["ok"],"n":[162.0]},"attendance_k8_all":{"y":["2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2021-22","2022-23","2023-24","2024-25"],"v":[0.94,0.944,0.9,0.892,0.9,0.9,0.903],"st":